After you've gotten PC nethack compiled and linked, if your exe file is
bigger than 540k, it will not work.  MSDOS is kind of stupid when it
comes to memory management.  An executable greater in length than available
memory (by a little) will be read into memory until DOS reaches the end
of free memory.  Then it WRAPS AROUND!!!  Your executable overwrites DOS,
and throws everything out of alignment. Thus, it doesn't work.

I realized this after my dad and I worked on nethack for about 3 hours,
and found the symbol table at the beginning of one of the important segments.

You must get the size of the executable below 540k.

I hope this helps,

